Installation
------------

Single-user install (default)
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

1. Extract the tarball into ~/iedb_tools and change into the tool folder:

    mkdir -p ~/iedb_tools
    tar -xvzf IEDB_NG_*-TOOL_VERSION.tar.gz -C ~/iedb_tools
    cd ~/iedb_tools/ng_{TOOL_NAME}-TOOL_VERSION

2. Install the dependencies into ./.venv, then write the .env file that the
tool reads at run time:

    uv sync
    ./configure

Multi-user / shared install
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

uv sync keeps Python under ~/.local/share/uv/python/, so a single-user
install works only for the user who ran it. To share one install, point uv
at world-readable folders before uv sync. An admin creates /apps/uv once.

    export UV_PYTHON_INSTALL_DIR=/apps/uv/python
    export UV_CACHE_DIR=/apps/uv/cache
    export UV_PYTHON_PREFERENCE=only-managed
    umask 0022
    uv sync
    ./configure

Usage
-----

The commands below start with uv run, which runs them in ./.venv without
activating it. To type plain python instead, run source .venv/bin/activate
first.

List the subcommands, then the options of predict. Each subcommand takes -h.

    uv run python src/run_{TOOL_EXEC_NAME}.py -h
    uv run python src/run_{TOOL_EXEC_NAME}.py predict -h

Run a prediction on a JSON input file. -o sets the output prefix, and -f sets
the format: tsv (the default) or json. <Replace the example input with a real
one, and describe the output.>

    echo '{"<parameter>": "<value>"}' > input.json
    uv run python src/run_{TOOL_EXEC_NAME}.py predict -j input.json -o output/result

For batch runs, preprocess splits an input into jobs and postprocess merges
their results. <Describe the batch workflow for {TOOL_NAME}, or delete this
paragraph.>
